WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.560
Hi guys! Tyler and I were sent out this past week

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:05.320
to visit Axel for the Make-a-Wish foundation,

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:07.380
uh it was a last minute trip, but we were happy to go

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:12.220
uh and when we got there we got to meet, Axel his whole family and the hospital staff

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:17.820
every one in his support  group and it was a really cool time because there was food, video games

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:21.680
and we just spent all day, pretty much spent just playing Rocket League and Skylanders

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:23.680
and he kicked our butts at Rocket league

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:27.820
real bad, either that or we're just playing bad at it

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.580
but it was a lot of fun and then Axel towards the end of the day

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:33.440
had something that he wanted to tell you guys

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:35.500
and I promised him I would put it into the video

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:37.220
so here's that message

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:41.360
So, we're here with Axel and Axel wanted to say something to you guys

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:44.540
Uh, You have any prepared statements, a speech of some sort?

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:53.540
No I just - thanks for always supporting Markiplier,

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:55.840
'cause I can't, I can't subscribe to him

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:58.860
since I don't have my own YouTube/Google account.

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:04.240
But if I did, I would, I would comment on every single of his videos,

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:08.260
and subscribe and like all his videos,

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:15.660
so thank you so much for, for helping Mark even though I can't.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:19.500
Aww (background giggles)

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:21.500
That's really sweet, thank you so much

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:24.940
It was really interesting to hear that and it's not what I expected him to say

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:29.840
because I've never heard it from that perspective before

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:34.280
where someone is an avid fan and yet they weren't able to support what I do

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:37.980
And I was just honoured, you know,

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:41.480
I was kinda humbled, because I get so much support and

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:43.480
it was a reminder that

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:47.660
I'm literally not here or I wouldn't be here

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:49.660
if it weren't for you guys and

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:51.660
I wouldn't be able where I am today

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:54.360
and I wouldn't be able to do what I wanna do

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:56.360
and I wouldn't be able to do these charity efforts

00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:59.740
and  I wouldn't be able to go out and visit people for their wishes,

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:01.740
if it weren't for you guys.

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:06.760
I just wanna thank you everyone for being there for me

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:09.080
and supporting what I do and

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:10.680
supporting what we do here

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:12.680
and just making it something

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:15.640
really, really special.

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:19.580
So anyway, I just wanna make this short and sweet

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:21.580
this video is mostly about Axel's message

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:23.240
so I'll leave it at that.

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:25.240
Just thank you everybody so much for watching

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:29.740
and as always, I will see you in the next video

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:31.740
Buh-Bye!

